WEBVTT

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:32.688
Just So Stories by Rudyard Kipling Copyright Black Cat Publishing The Elephants Child Part 1 The Elephants Child is a young elephant and he lives in the forest in Africa.

00:00:32.748 --> 00:00:39.866
He's grey and he's got big ears and his nose is small.

00:00:39.926 --> 00:00:45.209
He's a curious elephant and he asks a lot of questions.

00:00:45.269 --> 00:00:54.034
One hot summer day he asks his aunt ostrich, why have you got a lot of feathers?

00:00:54.094 --> 00:00:58.006
His aunt gets angry and hits him.

00:00:58.066 --> 00:01:06.251
He asks his tall uncle giraffe, Why have you got a lot of spots?

00:01:06.311 --> 00:01:10.024
His uncle gets angry and hits him.

00:01:10.084 --> 00:01:14.588
Then he asks his big aunt hippopotamus.

00:01:14.648 --> 00:01:18.842
Why have you got red eyes?

00:01:18.902 --> 00:01:22.705
His aunt gets angry and hits him.

00:01:22.765 --> 00:01:27.008
The elephant's child goes to his uncle Baboon.

00:01:27.068 --> 00:01:28.947
He asks him.

00:01:29.007 --> 00:01:32.455
Why are bananas good to eat?

00:01:32.515 --> 00:01:35.676
You eat them every day.

00:01:35.736 --> 00:01:40.578
His uncle gets angry and hits him too.

00:01:40.638 --> 00:01:48.120
One beautiful day, the elephant's child goes to the other elephants and asks a new question.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:52.191
What does the crocodile have for dinner?

00:01:52.251 --> 00:01:57.651
The other elephants get angry and say, Be quiet.

00:01:57.710 --> 00:02:01.511
Then they hit the elephant's child.

00:02:01.571 --> 00:02:09.158
When he sees the beautiful colo-colo bird, he asks, Can you help me?

00:02:09.218 --> 00:02:11.180
What do you want?

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:13.712
asks the colo-colo bird.

00:02:13.772 --> 00:02:17.354
What does the crocodile have for dinner?

00:02:17.414 --> 00:02:19.956
asks the elephant's child.

00:02:20.016 --> 00:02:24.130
Go to the green-limb purple river and find out.

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:26.818
Says the colo-colo bird.

00:02:26.878 --> 00:02:32.616
The next morning, the elephant's child sees some friends and talks to them.

00:02:32.676 --> 00:02:35.437
Good morning, my friends.

00:02:35.497 --> 00:02:37.587
Says the elephant's child.

00:02:37.647 --> 00:02:41.288
I'm going to the Limpup or River.

00:02:41.348 --> 00:02:46.249
I want to find out what the crocodile has for dinner.

00:02:46.309 --> 00:02:48.420
Good luck to you.

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.260
Say his friends.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:51.871
Thank you.

00:02:51.931 --> 00:02:53.822
He says happily.

00:02:53.882 --> 00:02:59.626
He takes six bananas and some other fruit and starts walking.

00:02:59.686 --> 00:03:04.639
One day, he sees a python sitting in a tall tree.

00:03:04.699 --> 00:03:07.581
Excuse me, python.

00:03:07.641 --> 00:03:09.452
Says the elephant's child.

00:03:09.512 --> 00:03:12.604
Does a crocodile live here?

00:03:12.664 --> 00:03:20.788
The python looks at the elephant's child and says, The crocodile lives in the green Limpopo River.

00:03:20.848 --> 00:03:23.661
What does he have for dinner?

00:03:23.721 --> 00:03:26.184
asks the elephant's child.

00:03:26.244 --> 00:03:32.598
The python gets angry and hits the elephant's child with his long tail.

00:03:32.658 --> 00:03:34.360
Oh dear.

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:36.712
The elephant's child thinks.

00:03:36.772 --> 00:03:39.834
Everyone is angry with me.

00:03:39.894 --> 00:03:43.818
I must go to the Limp-Bop-Bop River.

00:03:43.878 --> 00:03:50.002
He turns around and slowly goes away.

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:54.200
Part two.

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:58.828
The elephant's child arrives at the Limpopo River.

00:03:58.888 --> 00:04:03.292
He sees a new animal in the Big Green River.

00:04:03.352 --> 00:04:06.694
What a strange animal.

00:04:06.754 --> 00:04:07.965
He thinks.

00:04:08.025 --> 00:04:10.046
What is it?

00:04:10.106 --> 00:04:12.689
Excuse me.

00:04:12.749 --> 00:04:13.870
He asks.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:17.283
Does a crocodile live here?

00:04:17.342 --> 00:04:20.274
Yes, a little elephant.

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:23.568
Says the new animal in the Green River.

00:04:23.628 --> 00:04:26.691
I'm a crocodile.

00:04:26.751 --> 00:04:28.972
Oh, good.

00:04:29.032 --> 00:04:31.033
Says the elephant's child.

00:04:31.093 --> 00:04:35.605
Can you please tell me what you have for dinner?

00:04:35.664 --> 00:04:38.216
Yes, of course.

00:04:38.275 --> 00:04:40.936
Says the crocodile happily.

00:04:40.996 --> 00:04:45.858
Come close to me and I can tell you.

00:04:45.918 --> 00:04:50.320
The elephant's child goes close to the crocodile.

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:57.922
Today I'm going to have the elephant's child for dinner.

00:04:57.982 --> 00:05:00.423
He says laughing.

00:05:00.483 --> 00:05:04.054
He bites the elephant's child's little nose.

00:05:04.114 --> 00:05:06.525
Oh, my poor nose.

00:05:06.585 --> 00:05:08.345
Cries the elephant's child.

00:05:08.405 --> 00:05:09.896
What are you doing?

00:05:09.916 --> 00:05:14.967
The python sees everything and wants to help the elephant's child.

00:05:15.027 --> 00:05:23.078
He quickly goes to him and says, Pull hard, the crocodile wants to eat you and he's very strong.

00:05:23.138 --> 00:05:28.013
The python helps the elephant's child and they pull together.

00:05:28.073 --> 00:05:33.408
The crocodile pulls and the elephant's child and the python pull.

00:05:33.468 --> 00:05:37.652
The elephant's child's nose becomes very long.

00:05:37.712 --> 00:05:43.436
At last, the crocodile lets go and he is very angry.

00:05:43.496 --> 00:05:46.348
The elephant's child is free.

00:05:46.407 --> 00:05:48.788
Thank you, Python.

00:05:48.848 --> 00:05:51.229
Says the elephant's child happily.

00:05:51.289 --> 00:05:54.160
You're a good friend.

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:56.822
Your nose is very long now.

00:05:56.882 --> 00:05:59.343
Says the python looking at it.

00:05:59.402 --> 00:06:02.724
Oh dear, you're right.

00:06:02.784 --> 00:06:07.636
Says the elephant's child and he looks at his long nose.

00:06:07.696 --> 00:06:11.805
What can I do with this long nose?

00:06:11.865 --> 00:06:17.465
The python thinks for a moment and says, You can do a lot of things.

00:06:17.524 --> 00:06:19.666
Please tell me.

00:06:19.725 --> 00:06:21.666
Says the elephant's child.

00:06:21.726 --> 00:06:27.169
You can kill flies and you can eat green leaves from tall trees.

00:06:27.229 --> 00:06:33.182
You can have a cold shower with water from the river and you can hit other animals.

00:06:33.242 --> 00:06:36.684
Your new nose is very useful.

00:06:36.744 --> 00:06:38.464
You're right.

00:06:38.524 --> 00:06:41.806
I can do a lot of things with it.

00:06:41.866 --> 00:06:44.158
says the elephant's child.

00:06:44.218 --> 00:06:48.682
He goes home and shows the other elephants his new nose.

00:06:48.742 --> 00:06:51.314
Look at my new nose.

00:06:51.374 --> 00:06:55.617
He says, it's very long and useful.

00:06:55.676 --> 00:06:59.489
He tells them about all the things he can do with it.

00:06:59.549 --> 00:07:03.502
His friends are surprised and like it a lot.

00:07:03.562 --> 00:07:06.734
We want a new nose like yours.

00:07:06.794 --> 00:07:08.406
Say his friends.

00:07:08.466 --> 00:07:10.554
That's easy.

00:07:10.614 --> 00:07:12.663
says the elephant's child.

00:07:12.723 --> 00:07:17.194
Go to the crocodile at Limpapa River.

00:07:17.254 --> 00:07:22.106
He can give you a long new nose like mine.

00:07:22.166 --> 00:07:26.697
The elephants go to the green river and find the crocodile.

00:07:26.757 --> 00:07:32.899
Soon they all have long new noses and they are very happy.

00:07:32.959 --> 00:07:39.000
And this is how the elephant got his trunk.

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:43.892
Old man Kangaroo.

00:07:43.952 --> 00:07:50.945
The Kangaroo is a grey animal with four short legs and a long tail.

00:07:51.005 --> 00:07:53.576
He lives in Australia.

00:07:53.636 --> 00:07:57.178
He likes dancing and he's clever.

00:07:57.237 --> 00:08:03.600
One day, at six o'clock in the morning, the Kangaroo goes to the little magician.

00:08:03.660 --> 00:08:05.641
Good morning, little magician.

00:08:05.701 --> 00:08:07.442
Says Kangaroo.

00:08:07.502 --> 00:08:10.659
Please make me different from the other animals.

00:08:10.719 --> 00:08:11.816
What?

00:08:11.876 --> 00:08:14.707
Cries the little magician angrily.

00:08:14.767 --> 00:08:17.428
Go away Kangaroo.

00:08:17.488 --> 00:08:21.561
The Kangaroo goes away and has breakfast.

00:08:21.621 --> 00:08:25.854
At eight o'clock he goes to the middle magician.

00:08:25.914 --> 00:08:29.266
I want to be different from the other animals.

00:08:29.326 --> 00:08:31.066
Says the Kangaroo.

00:08:31.126 --> 00:08:33.588
And I want to be popular.

00:08:33.648 --> 00:08:36.549
Make me different and popular.

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:37.630
What?

00:08:37.690 --> 00:08:40.676
Cries the middle magician angrily.

00:08:40.736 --> 00:08:42.870
Go away.

00:08:42.931 --> 00:08:48.032
Before lunch, the kangaroo goes to the big magician.

00:08:48.092 --> 00:08:49.943
Hello, big magician.

00:08:50.003 --> 00:08:51.554
Says the kangaroo.

00:08:51.614 --> 00:08:53.715
Make me popular and different.

00:08:53.775 --> 00:08:56.736
I want the other animals to run after me.

00:08:56.796 --> 00:09:02.698
The big magician is having a bath, but looks at him and has an idea.

00:09:02.758 --> 00:09:04.389
All right, kangaroo.

00:09:04.449 --> 00:09:06.379
Says the big magician.

00:09:06.439 --> 00:09:08.403
Come here, dingo.

00:09:08.463 --> 00:09:11.887
The dingo goes to the big magician.

00:09:11.947 --> 00:09:13.828
What must I do?

00:09:13.888 --> 00:09:15.708
asks the dingo.

00:09:15.768 --> 00:09:17.879
Do you see that grey animal?

00:09:17.939 --> 00:09:19.840
asks the big magician.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:21.520
Yes, I do.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:22.911
Says the dingo.

00:09:22.971 --> 00:09:24.781
You must run after him.

00:09:24.841 --> 00:09:27.182
Says the big magician.

00:09:27.242 --> 00:09:30.943
The dingo starts running after the kangaroo.

00:09:31.003 --> 00:09:38.934
The two animals run everywhere, through the green trees of the forest and through the hot desert.

00:09:38.994 --> 00:09:43.166
They run up and down the hills and the mountains.

00:09:43.226 --> 00:09:48.719
They run through the tall green grass and the short brown grass.

00:09:48.779 --> 00:09:52.712
At first the kangaroo likes running fast.

00:09:52.772 --> 00:09:55.253
He thinks it's great fun.

00:09:55.313 --> 00:09:59.696
But after a few hours he gets tired.

00:09:59.756 --> 00:10:02.228
I can't stop running now.

00:10:02.288 --> 00:10:03.828
Thanks the kangaroo.

00:10:03.888 --> 00:10:06.438
The dingo wants to catch me.

00:10:06.498 --> 00:10:11.068
The dingo likes running fast, but he is tired too.

00:10:11.128 --> 00:10:13.189
I can't stop running now.

00:10:13.249 --> 00:10:14.800
Thanks the dingo.

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.592
But I'm hungry.

00:10:16.652 --> 00:10:21.354
The kangaroo and the dingo run all over Australia.

00:10:21.414 --> 00:10:25.778
When they get to the Walgong River, there is no bridge.

00:10:25.838 --> 00:10:28.579
The kangaroo stops running.

00:10:28.640 --> 00:10:31.341
How can I cross the river?

00:10:31.401 --> 00:10:33.072
Thanks the kangaroo.

00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:37.334
There is no bridge, so I must hop across.

00:10:37.394 --> 00:10:41.875
He hops across the river and gets to the other side.

00:10:41.935 --> 00:10:43.436
That's easy.

00:10:43.496 --> 00:10:44.667
He thinks.

00:10:44.727 --> 00:10:47.618
It's easy to hop and I like it.

00:10:47.678 --> 00:10:52.802
He pulls up his front legs and uses his tail to help him.

00:10:52.862 --> 00:10:55.723
Then he hops again and again.

00:10:55.743 --> 00:10:58.044
I love hopping.

00:10:58.104 --> 00:10:59.365
He thinks.

00:10:59.425 --> 00:11:04.796
So he hops through the deserts of Australia and the dingo follows him.

00:11:04.856 --> 00:11:07.176
When is he going to stop?

00:11:07.236 --> 00:11:09.058
Thinks the dingo.

00:11:09.118 --> 00:11:11.260
I'm very hungry.

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:17.634
At five o'clock in the afternoon, the kangaroo and the dingo see the big magician.

00:11:17.694 --> 00:11:21.548
He is sitting in the river, having another bath.

00:11:21.608 --> 00:11:25.360
They stop and sit by the river.

00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:28.203
I'm very tired.

00:11:28.263 --> 00:11:30.064
Says the kangaroo.

00:11:30.124 --> 00:11:32.461
And I'm very hungry.

00:11:32.521 --> 00:11:33.867
Says the dingo.

00:11:33.927 --> 00:11:35.919
Why don't you thank the dingo?

00:11:35.979 --> 00:11:38.922
The big magician asks the kangaroo.

00:11:38.982 --> 00:11:40.113
Thank him.

00:11:40.173 --> 00:11:41.714
Says the kangaroo.

00:11:41.774 --> 00:11:42.706
Why?

00:11:42.766 --> 00:11:44.417
You want to be different.

00:11:44.477 --> 00:11:46.179
Says the big magician.

00:11:46.239 --> 00:11:47.340
No, you're different.

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.702
Look at your legs and your long tail.

00:11:49.762 --> 00:11:52.444
But my long legs are funny.

00:11:52.504 --> 00:11:55.875
Says the kangaroo, looking at his legs.

00:11:55.935 --> 00:11:58.954
Do you want the dingo to run after you until midnight?

00:11:59.014 --> 00:12:00.716
Ask the big magician.

00:12:00.776 --> 00:12:01.386
No.

00:12:01.446 --> 00:12:02.267
No.

00:12:02.326 --> 00:12:04.048
Says the kangaroo.

00:12:04.108 --> 00:12:06.760
My legs and long tail are fine.

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:07.800
I like them.

00:12:07.860 --> 00:12:10.392
But now I'm very hungry.

00:12:10.452 --> 00:12:11.702
I am too.

00:12:11.762 --> 00:12:13.664
Says the dingo.

00:12:13.724 --> 00:12:17.456
What can I have for dinner?

00:12:17.516 --> 00:12:18.987
Ask me tomorrow.

00:12:19.047 --> 00:12:21.400
Says the big magician.

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:28.365
So the kangaroo and the dingo are tired and hungry in the middle of Australia.

00:12:28.425 --> 00:12:30.896
They look at each other.

00:12:30.956 --> 00:12:33.407
All of this is your fault.

00:12:33.467 --> 00:12:34.737
Says the dingo.

00:12:34.797 --> 00:12:36.118
Now it's not.

00:12:36.178 --> 00:12:37.508
Says kangaroo.

00:12:37.568 --> 00:12:38.948
It's your fault.

00:12:39.008 --> 00:12:40.119
You're wrong.

00:12:40.179 --> 00:12:41.429
Says the dingo.

00:12:41.489 --> 00:12:43.080
It's your fault.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:49.188
And at midnight, they are still arguing.

00:12:49.248 --> 00:13:00.168
The Animals of Australia Australia has a lot of animals that you can't find in other places in the world.

00:13:00.228 --> 00:13:02.679
Let's have a look at some of them.

00:13:02.739 --> 00:13:09.392
The Kangaroo The Kangaroo is probably the most popular animal of Australia.

00:13:09.452 --> 00:13:11.822
The Kangaroo is a marsupial.

00:13:11.882 --> 00:13:15.404
That means that it carries its young in a special pouch.

00:13:15.464 --> 00:13:18.728
A baby kangaroo is called a joey.

00:13:18.788 --> 00:13:24.844
When a joey is born, it is very small, only about two centimeters long.

00:13:24.904 --> 00:13:30.046
It lives in its mother's pouch for nine months before leaving it.

00:13:30.106 --> 00:13:33.317
The kangaroo is a herbivore.

00:13:33.377 --> 00:13:38.349
It eats only grass and plants and does not eat meat.

00:13:38.409 --> 00:13:43.651
It can grow to two meters and weigh around 90 kilograms.

00:13:43.711 --> 00:13:50.517
It moves about by hopping Some kangaroos are red, and some are grey.

00:13:50.577 --> 00:13:54.160
They live in all parts of Australia.

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.932
The koala.

00:13:56.992 --> 00:14:04.710
The koala is often called the koala bear because it looks like a small bear, but it is not a bear.

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:06.570
It is a marsupia.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:11.054
It lives in trees and does not like staying on the ground.

00:14:11.114 --> 00:14:13.472
It eats leaves and fruit.

00:14:13.531 --> 00:14:18.738
The koala sleeps most of the day in trees, and usually eats at night.

00:14:18.798 --> 00:14:23.319
It lives in eastern and southern Australia, near the sea.

00:14:23.379 --> 00:14:25.439
The emu.

00:14:25.499 --> 00:14:29.220
The emu is a very big bird in Australia.

00:14:29.280 --> 00:14:31.821
It is about two metres tall.

00:14:31.881 --> 00:14:35.611
It does not fly, but it can run very fast.

00:14:35.671 --> 00:14:38.222
Around 50 kilometres an hour.

00:14:38.282 --> 00:14:43.566
It lives in all areas of Australia, but it doesn't like forests.

00:14:43.626 --> 00:14:47.611
It eats plants and insects.

00:14:47.671 --> 00:14:50.522
The platypus.

00:14:50.582 --> 00:14:57.518
The platypus lives in small rivers in eastern Australia and is an excellent swimmer.

00:14:57.578 --> 00:15:00.160
It has a very strange nose.

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:02.912
This looks like a duck's mouth.

00:15:02.972 --> 00:15:06.324
It can also live in and out of water.

00:15:06.384 --> 00:15:10.147
It sleeps during the day and moves at night.

00:15:10.206 --> 00:15:13.470
It eats small animals and insects.

00:15:13.530 --> 00:15:17.832
It is about the size of a cat.

00:15:17.892 --> 00:15:22.704
How the leopard got his spots.

00:15:22.764 --> 00:15:25.734
Part 1.

00:15:25.794 --> 00:15:33.938
All the animals of the hot African savanna are a dark yellow or light brown colour.

00:15:33.998 --> 00:15:38.339
They are the same colour as the grass and trees around them.

00:15:38.399 --> 00:15:44.022
It's difficult to see the dark yellow giraffe and the light brown zebra.

00:15:44.082 --> 00:15:52.565
And the leopard is very difficult to see, because he is exactly the same colour as the savanna.

00:15:52.626 --> 00:15:57.638
The leopard often hunts giraffes and zebras with a young man.

00:15:57.698 --> 00:16:00.730
They are both very good hunters.

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:05.162
All the giraffes and zebras are afraid of them.

00:16:05.222 --> 00:16:12.228
I'm afraid of the leopard because I can't see him and he always surprises me.

00:16:12.288 --> 00:16:13.698
Says the Zebra.

00:16:13.758 --> 00:16:14.939
You're right.

00:16:14.999 --> 00:16:16.400
Says the giraffe.

00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:18.232
I'm afraid of him too.

00:16:18.292 --> 00:16:21.704
But I'm also very afraid of the man.

00:16:21.764 --> 00:16:24.766
We're always in danger here.

00:16:24.826 --> 00:16:26.257
Says the Zebra.

00:16:26.317 --> 00:16:28.478
Why don't we go somewhere else?

00:16:28.538 --> 00:16:29.509
Yes.

00:16:29.569 --> 00:16:31.450
Let's go away.

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:32.812
Says the giraffe.

00:16:32.872 --> 00:16:34.222
Follow me.

00:16:34.282 --> 00:16:38.756
So the giraffe and the zebra go to a big forest.

00:16:38.816 --> 00:16:42.758
This is a lovely forest with beautiful colours.

00:16:42.818 --> 00:16:45.000
Says the giraffe happily.

00:16:45.060 --> 00:16:49.412
Yes, everything is green, brown or black.

00:16:49.472 --> 00:16:51.524
And it's not hot here.

00:16:51.584 --> 00:16:52.954
Says the zebra.

00:16:53.014 --> 00:16:54.776
I like it.

00:16:54.836 --> 00:16:59.168
There are a lot of tall green trees in the forest.

00:16:59.228 --> 00:17:03.342
The trees and plants make strange shadows.

00:17:03.402 --> 00:17:07.396
They fall on the animals and they don't go away.

00:17:07.456 --> 00:17:09.137
Look at me.

00:17:09.197 --> 00:17:10.678
Says the giraffe.

00:17:10.738 --> 00:17:13.380
I've got some patches on my body.

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:15.161
Yes, you have.

00:17:15.221 --> 00:17:16.562
Says the zebra.

00:17:16.622 --> 00:17:18.373
They are beautiful.

00:17:18.433 --> 00:17:22.876
And you've got some wonderful stripes on your body.

00:17:22.936 --> 00:17:24.747
Says the giraffe.

00:17:24.807 --> 00:17:28.820
The zebra looks at his body and sees the stripes.

00:17:28.880 --> 00:17:31.620
He likes them and he's happy.

00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:34.550
Now we can hide from the leopard.

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:36.041
Says the giraffe.

00:17:36.101 --> 00:17:41.634
He can smell us, and he can hear us, but he can't see us.

00:17:41.694 --> 00:17:47.456
The zebra and the giraffe are happy and safe in the big forest.

00:17:47.516 --> 00:17:54.040
The leopard and the man go hunting, but they can't find the zebra and the giraffe.

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:56.861
Where are the zebra and the giraffe?

00:17:56.921 --> 00:17:58.490
Asks the man.

00:17:58.550 --> 00:18:03.960
I can smell them, and I can hear them, but I can't see them.

00:18:04.019 --> 00:18:05.760
Says the leopard.

00:18:05.820 --> 00:18:10.541
They go and ask a clever baboon called Bhavian.

00:18:10.601 --> 00:18:13.662
Where are the zebra and the giraffe?

00:18:13.722 --> 00:18:15.162
Asks the leopard.

00:18:15.222 --> 00:18:18.234
We can't find them and we're hungry.

00:18:18.294 --> 00:18:21.874
You must go through the big green forest.

00:18:21.934 --> 00:18:23.846
Said Bhavian.

00:18:23.906 --> 00:18:28.050
You can find them there, and you can look for spots too.

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:29.331
Spots?

00:18:29.391 --> 00:18:30.852
asks the leopard.

00:18:30.912 --> 00:18:32.303
Yes, spots.

00:18:32.363 --> 00:18:34.204
Says Bavian.

00:18:34.264 --> 00:18:36.026
I don't understand.

00:18:36.086 --> 00:18:37.417
Says the leopard.

00:18:37.477 --> 00:18:41.490
When you're in the green forest, look for spots.

00:18:41.550 --> 00:18:43.632
Says Bavian.

00:18:43.692 --> 00:18:48.946
The leopard and the man go to the forest, but they can't find the animals.

00:18:49.006 --> 00:18:50.877
What a strange place.

00:18:50.937 --> 00:18:52.148
Says the leopard.

00:18:52.208 --> 00:18:56.621
Yes, it's dark, but it's full of spots of light.

00:18:56.681 --> 00:18:58.172
Says the man.

00:18:58.232 --> 00:19:01.864
Are these the spots Bhavyan talks about?

00:19:01.924 --> 00:19:03.275
Asks the leopard.

00:19:03.335 --> 00:19:04.546
Perhaps.

00:19:04.606 --> 00:19:05.996
Says the man.

00:19:06.057 --> 00:19:11.270
I can smell a giraffe, and I can hear a giraffe.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:12.391
Says the man.

00:19:12.451 --> 00:19:14.362
But I can't see it.

00:19:14.422 --> 00:19:19.215
And I can smell a zebra, and I can hear a zebra.

00:19:19.275 --> 00:19:20.527
Says the leopard.

00:19:20.587 --> 00:19:22.799
But I can't see it.

00:19:22.859 --> 00:19:25.420
They look around the forest.

00:19:25.481 --> 00:19:27.502
Why can't we see them?

00:19:27.562 --> 00:19:29.052
Ask the man.

00:19:29.112 --> 00:19:31.404
That's a good question.

00:19:31.464 --> 00:19:34.816
Says the leopard.

00:19:34.876 --> 00:19:38.918
Part two.

00:19:38.978 --> 00:19:42.820
I know the animals are here somewhere.

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:44.370
Says the leopard.

00:19:44.431 --> 00:19:46.692
But I can't see them.

00:19:46.752 --> 00:19:49.290
Let's wait until the night.

00:19:49.350 --> 00:19:50.577
All right.

00:19:50.637 --> 00:19:52.108
Says the man.

00:19:52.168 --> 00:19:54.948
They sit down and wait.

00:19:55.008 --> 00:20:00.609
When it is dark, they hear and smell the zebra and the giraffe.

00:20:00.669 --> 00:20:03.580
The man catches the giraffe.

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:05.430
Now you're mine.

00:20:05.490 --> 00:20:07.000
He says happily.

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:09.370
And the leopard catches the zebra.

00:20:09.431 --> 00:20:11.331
And now you're mine.

00:20:11.391 --> 00:20:14.101
He shouts, looking at the zebra.

00:20:14.161 --> 00:20:17.422
But there's something strange about these animals.

00:20:17.482 --> 00:20:19.004
You're right.

00:20:19.064 --> 00:20:20.325
Says the man.

00:20:20.385 --> 00:20:23.768
Let's wait until morning and see.

00:20:23.828 --> 00:20:29.193
The next morning, the leopard and the man look at the two animals carefully.

00:20:29.253 --> 00:20:30.664
What's this?

00:20:30.724 --> 00:20:32.306
Says the leopard.

00:20:32.366 --> 00:20:34.698
A zebra with stripes.

00:20:34.758 --> 00:20:37.080
And what's this?

00:20:37.140 --> 00:20:38.381
Says the man.

00:20:38.441 --> 00:20:41.574
A giraffe with patches?

00:20:41.634 --> 00:20:45.294
The leopard and the man are very surprised.

00:20:45.354 --> 00:20:48.624
The giraffe and the zebra laugh.

00:20:48.684 --> 00:20:51.184
Why are you different?

00:20:51.244 --> 00:20:55.386
Asks the leopard, looking at the zebra and the giraffe.

00:20:55.446 --> 00:20:58.918
Please let us go, and we can show you our trick.

00:20:58.978 --> 00:21:00.388
Says the giraffe.

00:21:00.448 --> 00:21:02.799
Yes, show us.

00:21:02.859 --> 00:21:05.610
Say the leopard and the man.

00:21:05.670 --> 00:21:10.502
The giraffe and the zebra go under the tall green trees.

00:21:10.562 --> 00:21:15.071
Suddenly, the leopard and the man can't see them anymore.

00:21:15.131 --> 00:21:16.909
Where are you?

00:21:16.969 --> 00:21:18.540
Ask the man.

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:22.662
The giraffe and the zebra laugh.

00:21:22.722 --> 00:21:27.525
I can hear you laugh, but I can't see you.

00:21:27.585 --> 00:21:29.596
Says the leopard.

00:21:29.656 --> 00:21:31.928
Laughs the giraffe.

00:21:31.988 --> 00:21:34.309
Where's your breakfast now?

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:38.592
The leopard and the man don't know where they are.

00:21:38.652 --> 00:21:42.244
We're here under the tall trees.

00:21:42.304 --> 00:21:44.033
Says the zebra.

00:21:44.093 --> 00:21:49.624
But it's almost impossible to see us, because we look like the shadows of the forest.

00:21:49.684 --> 00:21:50.705
You're right.

00:21:50.765 --> 00:21:52.226
Says the leopard.

00:21:52.286 --> 00:21:54.938
That's a very good trick.

00:21:54.998 --> 00:21:56.558
Says the man.

00:21:56.618 --> 00:21:59.120
I think I need spots too.

00:21:59.181 --> 00:22:00.952
Says the leopard.

00:22:01.012 --> 00:22:05.174
That's what Babian says and he's clever.

00:22:05.234 --> 00:22:07.165
It's a good idea.

00:22:07.226 --> 00:22:08.266
Says the man.

00:22:08.326 --> 00:22:11.648
It's more difficult to see you with spots.

00:22:11.708 --> 00:22:17.200
The leopard goes into the forest and its shadows fall on him.

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:22.494
Now he has dark spots on his body and they don't go away.

00:22:22.554 --> 00:22:28.419
You've got some lovely dark spots all over your body leopard.

00:22:28.479 --> 00:22:29.780
Says the man.

00:22:29.840 --> 00:22:31.161
I like them.

00:22:31.221 --> 00:22:32.502
Says the leopard.

00:22:32.562 --> 00:22:36.951
Now I can hide in the forest like the Giraffe and the Zebra.

00:22:37.011 --> 00:22:37.968
Yes.

00:22:38.028 --> 00:22:39.268
Says the man.

00:22:39.328 --> 00:22:42.910
Now, no one can find you in the forest.

00:22:42.971 --> 00:22:44.741
I'm very happy.

00:22:44.802 --> 00:22:46.322
Says the leopard.

00:22:46.382 --> 00:22:48.213
And I'm hungry.

00:22:48.274 --> 00:22:49.994
Let's go hunting.

00:22:50.054 --> 00:22:50.945
Yes.

00:22:51.005 --> 00:22:52.336
Good idea.

00:22:52.396 --> 00:22:55.578
Says the man.

00:22:55.638 --> 00:23:00.054
Listening activity.

00:23:00.114 --> 00:23:02.218
Good morning.

00:23:02.279 --> 00:23:05.990
I'm Sam Wilson, the Safari Tour Guide.

00:23:06.050 --> 00:23:09.722
The Monday morning tour starts in 10 minutes.

00:23:09.782 --> 00:23:12.193
That's at half past 9.

00:23:12.254 --> 00:23:16.866
On Sundays and holidays, we start at 10 o'clock.

00:23:16.926 --> 00:23:21.722
Please buy your tickets now at the ticket office on your right.

00:23:21.782 --> 00:23:28.431
Adults pay 15 euros and children between 8 and 16 pay 10 euros.

00:23:28.491 --> 00:23:33.204
However, children under the age of 8 can come for free.

00:23:33.264 --> 00:23:35.466
And now the good news.

00:23:35.526 --> 00:23:40.840
Families with 2 or more children pay only 35 euros.

00:23:40.900 --> 00:23:50.196
Everyone on the tour must have a hat and a pair of sunglasses because the sun is very hot in the afternoon.

00:23:50.256 --> 00:23:53.308
Actually, it's always hot here.

00:23:53.368 --> 00:23:57.590
And don't forget to bring a bottle of water too.

00:23:57.650 --> 00:24:02.763
Our Safari tour starts at the Safari National Park entrance.

00:24:02.823 --> 00:24:07.054
This National Park is the biggest in the area.

00:24:07.114 --> 00:24:12.636
We're going to ride for about 8 miles in the hot savannah during the morning.

00:24:12.696 --> 00:24:20.100
In the savannah we're going to see leopards, zebras, giraffes, elephants and hippos.

00:24:20.161 --> 00:24:22.852
Get your cameras ready.

00:24:22.912 --> 00:24:27.845
At half past noon we're going to stop for a short lunch break.

00:24:27.905 --> 00:24:31.813
There are free sandwiches and drinks for everyone.

00:24:31.873 --> 00:24:37.952
In the afternoon, we're going to ride for six miles in the jungle near the Green River.

00:24:38.012 --> 00:24:48.780
This is very exciting because we're going to see monkeys, baboons, crocodiles, snakes and different kinds of African birds.

00:24:48.840 --> 00:24:55.686
Please don't touch the animals because it can be dangerous.

00:24:55.746 --> 00:25:00.714
How the whale got his throat.

00:25:00.774 --> 00:25:05.303
The whale is a big animal and he lives in the sea.

00:25:05.363 --> 00:25:10.025
He is always hungry and eats many different fish and sea animals.

00:25:10.085 --> 00:25:16.938
He doesn't have a throat and this means he can eat very big things as well as very small things.

00:25:16.998 --> 00:25:22.091
A very small fish called the little fish also lives in the sea.

00:25:22.151 --> 00:25:24.072
He is clever.

00:25:24.132 --> 00:25:28.014
The whale is eating all the fish in the sea.

00:25:28.074 --> 00:25:29.774
The little fish thinks.

00:25:29.834 --> 00:25:31.085
I'm afraid.

00:25:31.105 --> 00:25:34.127
I don't want him to eat me.

00:25:34.188 --> 00:25:37.280
I must hide behind his ear.

00:25:37.340 --> 00:25:43.296
But suddenly the whale stands up on his big tail and sees the little fish.

00:25:43.356 --> 00:25:45.548
I'm hungry.

00:25:45.608 --> 00:25:48.350
Says the whale in a loud voice.

00:25:48.410 --> 00:25:50.342
What's this?

00:25:50.402 --> 00:25:52.744
A little fish.

00:25:52.804 --> 00:25:55.076
Hello, great whale.

00:25:55.136 --> 00:25:57.268
Says the little fish.

00:25:57.328 --> 00:25:59.009
Eating man.

00:25:59.029 --> 00:26:01.640
Hmm, I don't know.

00:26:01.700 --> 00:26:05.052
Says the whale, looking at the little fish.

00:26:05.112 --> 00:26:08.934
I prefer dolphins or sharks.

00:26:08.994 --> 00:26:11.796
What is man like?

00:26:11.856 --> 00:26:15.517
Oh, man is very good.

00:26:15.577 --> 00:26:17.588
Says the clever little fish.

00:26:17.648 --> 00:26:19.059
Really?

00:26:19.119 --> 00:26:20.680
Says the whale.

00:26:20.740 --> 00:26:21.880
Yes.

00:26:21.940 --> 00:26:23.351
Says the little fish.

00:26:23.411 --> 00:26:25.380
Believe me.

00:26:25.440 --> 00:26:28.570
Can you find a man for me?"

00:26:28.630 --> 00:26:30.250
asks the whale.

00:26:30.310 --> 00:26:32.552
Of course I can!

00:26:32.612 --> 00:26:34.334
Says the little fish.

00:26:34.394 --> 00:26:42.219
You must swim to the north, and in the middle of the sea there is a young sailor on a raft.

00:26:42.279 --> 00:26:46.462
He's wearing blue trousers and breezes.

00:26:46.522 --> 00:26:47.753
Good!

00:26:47.813 --> 00:26:49.164
Let's go!

00:26:49.224 --> 00:26:50.784
Says the whale.

00:26:50.845 --> 00:26:54.517
The whale and the little fish swim across the sea.

00:26:54.577 --> 00:26:58.621
Soon the whale sees the sailor sitting on a raft.

00:26:58.681 --> 00:27:02.685
Good, I'm very hungry.

00:27:02.745 --> 00:27:04.016
Says the whale.

00:27:04.077 --> 00:27:10.262
He opens his big mouth and eats the young sailor and the raft.

00:27:10.322 --> 00:27:13.035
Says the whale.

00:27:13.095 --> 00:27:16.226
Man is very good.

00:27:16.286 --> 00:27:20.648
The sailor and his raft are inside the whale's stomach.

00:27:20.708 --> 00:27:22.700
What's happening to me?

00:27:22.760 --> 00:27:24.202
Thinks the sailor.

00:27:24.262 --> 00:27:25.764
He is afraid.

00:27:25.824 --> 00:27:27.535
Where am I?

00:27:27.595 --> 00:27:30.878
It's warm and dark in here.

00:27:30.938 --> 00:27:32.610
Oh, no.

00:27:32.670 --> 00:27:34.772
I'm inside a whale.

00:27:34.832 --> 00:27:36.293
What can I do?

00:27:36.313 --> 00:27:40.437
The sailor is very clever and looks around.

00:27:40.497 --> 00:27:42.372
He starts thinking.

00:27:42.432 --> 00:27:45.248
This whale can't eat me.

00:27:45.308 --> 00:27:46.948
He says angrily.

00:27:47.009 --> 00:27:52.251
He starts jumping, kicking and dancing inside the whale's stomach.

00:27:52.311 --> 00:27:56.414
The whale is very unhappy and feels ill.

00:27:56.474 --> 00:28:00.596
I've got a terrible stomach ache.

00:28:00.656 --> 00:28:03.337
Says the unhappy whale.

00:28:03.398 --> 00:28:05.508
I'm sorry whale.

00:28:05.568 --> 00:28:07.260
Says the little fish.

00:28:07.320 --> 00:28:10.221
What's the sailor doing?

00:28:10.281 --> 00:28:12.369
Asks the whale.

00:28:12.429 --> 00:28:15.288
Do you know little fish?

00:28:15.348 --> 00:28:17.158
I don't know.

00:28:17.219 --> 00:28:18.970
Says the little fish.

00:28:19.029 --> 00:28:24.323
The sailor continues jumping, kicking and dancing inside the whale's stomach.

00:28:24.383 --> 00:28:24.933
Oh!

00:28:24.994 --> 00:28:26.364
Says the whale.

00:28:26.424 --> 00:28:28.385
I feel sick.

00:28:28.446 --> 00:28:31.638
I'm going to ask the sailor to come out.

00:28:31.698 --> 00:28:33.469
Says the little fish.

00:28:33.529 --> 00:28:35.050
Thank you.

00:28:35.110 --> 00:28:37.092
That's a good idea.

00:28:37.152 --> 00:28:38.772
Says the whale.

00:28:38.832 --> 00:28:41.304
Please come out.

00:28:41.364 --> 00:28:43.330
Cries the little fish.

00:28:43.390 --> 00:28:44.884
What?

00:28:44.944 --> 00:28:46.646
Answers the sailor.

00:28:46.706 --> 00:28:50.538
The rail's got a terrible stomachache.

00:28:50.598 --> 00:28:52.239
Says the little fish.

00:28:52.299 --> 00:28:55.390
Please come out right now.

00:28:55.451 --> 00:28:56.571
No.

00:28:56.631 --> 00:28:58.622
I'm not coming out.

00:28:58.683 --> 00:29:00.654
Says the sailor angrily.

00:29:00.714 --> 00:29:04.466
You must take me home to England first.

00:29:04.526 --> 00:29:06.608
All right.

00:29:06.668 --> 00:29:09.318
Says the poor whale.

00:29:09.378 --> 00:29:12.304
I can take you home.

00:29:12.364 --> 00:29:16.529
The whale and the little fish start swimming fast.

00:29:16.589 --> 00:29:19.000
They swim across the sea to England.

00:29:19.060 --> 00:29:26.842
While the whale and the little fish swim, the sailor breaks up the raft and ties the pieces together with his braces.

00:29:26.902 --> 00:29:33.084
When they get to the beach in England, the sailor has a big surprise for the whale.

00:29:33.144 --> 00:29:37.395
Whale, open your big mouth.

00:29:37.455 --> 00:29:41.246
Says the sailor, I want to get out.

00:29:41.307 --> 00:29:45.850
The whale opens his mouth, and the sailor walks out.

00:29:45.910 --> 00:29:49.422
But he leaves his raft in the whale's mouth.

00:29:49.482 --> 00:29:55.578
Now, my raft is your throat, and you can never eat men again.

00:29:55.638 --> 00:29:57.018
Says the sailor.

00:29:57.078 --> 00:30:01.482
With this raft, you can only eat very small fish.

00:30:01.542 --> 00:30:02.904
What?

00:30:02.964 --> 00:30:05.996
Only very small fish.

00:30:06.056 --> 00:30:08.168
Says the whale angrily.

00:30:08.228 --> 00:30:12.760
I don't want this in my throat.

00:30:12.820 --> 00:30:18.933
The whale cuffs and cuffs, but the raft doesn't move.

00:30:18.993 --> 00:30:22.753
He is very sad and slowly swims away.

00:30:22.813 --> 00:30:27.104
The sailor is on the beach and watches the whale swim away.

00:30:27.164 --> 00:30:29.064
Goodbye whale.

00:30:29.124 --> 00:30:30.885
Says the sailor happily.

00:30:30.945 --> 00:30:33.805
Now you can't eat men anymore.

00:30:33.865 --> 00:30:39.146
Men aren't nice and they give me a stomach ache.

00:30:39.206 --> 00:30:40.786
Says the whale.

00:30:40.846 --> 00:30:46.368
Small fish are much better.

00:30:46.428 --> 00:30:49.880
Whales.

00:30:49.940 --> 00:30:52.872
What do you know about whales?

00:30:52.932 --> 00:30:55.634
Here are some interesting facts.

00:30:55.694 --> 00:30:59.406
Whales live in the sea, but they are not fish.

00:30:59.466 --> 00:31:00.557
They are mammals.

00:31:00.617 --> 00:31:02.728
They need air to live.

00:31:02.788 --> 00:31:07.241
They must come up to the top of the water often to get air.

00:31:07.301 --> 00:31:12.114
They breathe air in and out through the blowhole on their back.

00:31:12.174 --> 00:31:16.887
When whales sleep, they stay on the top of the water.

00:31:16.947 --> 00:31:19.978
The biggest whale is the blue whale.

00:31:20.038 --> 00:31:25.483
It is around 30 metres long and weighs about 200 tonnes.

00:31:25.543 --> 00:31:31.827
Whales swim by moving their tails up and down and by using their flippers.

00:31:31.888 --> 00:31:35.300
Their flippers help them to turn around.

00:31:35.360 --> 00:31:39.844
Whales make a lot of noise because they talk to each other.

00:31:39.904 --> 00:31:44.799
Their underwater sounds can travel very far.

00:31:44.860 --> 00:31:48.314
Wales usually live in groups.

00:31:48.374 --> 00:31:55.229
A baby whale is called a calf, plural, calves.

00:31:55.289 --> 00:31:58.982
Wales move from one place to another.

00:31:59.042 --> 00:32:04.956
During the warm summer months, they eat a lot because they get ready for the winter.

00:32:05.017 --> 00:32:13.000
In the autumn, they start moving south to warm places, and in the spring, they move north.

00:32:13.060 --> 00:32:17.640
The killer whale is a very popular and dangerous whale.

00:32:17.700 --> 00:32:20.322
Here's some information about it.

00:32:20.383 --> 00:32:22.814
The killer whale.

00:32:22.875 --> 00:32:24.366
Name.

00:32:24.426 --> 00:32:25.486
Orca.

00:32:25.547 --> 00:32:27.668
Or killer whale.

00:32:27.728 --> 00:32:29.120
Color.

00:32:29.180 --> 00:32:31.302
Black and white.

00:32:31.362 --> 00:32:32.792
Size.

00:32:32.852 --> 00:32:38.046
Around 8 meters for males and 7 meters for females.

00:32:38.106 --> 00:32:39.716
Lives.

00:32:39.776 --> 00:32:49.086
in all major oceans from the arctic areas of Alaska, Canada, Scandinavia and Russia to the warm oceans in the south.

00:32:49.146 --> 00:32:53.328
They usually live in groups of around 40 whales.

00:32:53.388 --> 00:32:58.040
The killer whale can live for 30 to 50 years.

00:32:58.100 --> 00:33:06.440
Eats, fish and other sea animals are very dangerous predator.

00:33:06.500 --> 00:33:11.150
How the camel got his hump.

00:33:11.211 --> 00:33:17.857
The horse, the dog and the ox work for the farmer, but the camel does not.

00:33:17.917 --> 00:33:21.380
He has a long neck and long legs.

00:33:21.440 --> 00:33:25.674
He lives alone in the desert and doesn't want to work.

00:33:25.734 --> 00:33:32.643
He eats and sleeps, and when someone speaks to him, he says, humph.

00:33:32.703 --> 00:33:36.808
On Monday morning, the horse goes to see the camel.

00:33:36.868 --> 00:33:37.789
Camel?

00:33:37.849 --> 00:33:39.090
Says the horse.

00:33:39.150 --> 00:33:41.852
Come and work like all the other animals.

00:33:41.912 --> 00:33:45.315
I carry men on my back and work hard all day.

00:33:45.375 --> 00:33:46.526
Humph!

00:33:46.586 --> 00:33:50.190
Says the camel and the horse goes away.

00:33:50.250 --> 00:33:54.216
On Tuesday morning, the dog goes to see the camel.

00:33:54.276 --> 00:33:55.259
Camel.

00:33:55.319 --> 00:33:56.460
Says the dog.

00:33:56.520 --> 00:33:58.871
Camel worked like all the other animals.

00:33:58.931 --> 00:34:01.152
I guard the farmer's house.

00:34:01.212 --> 00:34:03.993
I work hard day and night.

00:34:04.054 --> 00:34:05.154
Humpf.

00:34:05.214 --> 00:34:09.056
Says the camel and the dog goes away.

00:34:09.116 --> 00:34:13.408
On Wednesday the big ox goes to see the camel.

00:34:13.468 --> 00:34:14.558
Camel?

00:34:14.618 --> 00:34:16.339
Says the big ox.

00:34:16.399 --> 00:34:18.400
Come and work for the farmer.

00:34:18.460 --> 00:34:21.251
I work hard in the country all day.

00:34:21.311 --> 00:34:22.595
Humpf.

00:34:22.654 --> 00:34:26.670
Says the camel, and the ox goes away.

00:34:26.730 --> 00:34:31.073
The animals go and tell the farmer about the lazy camel.

00:34:31.133 --> 00:34:33.554
The camel is very lazy.

00:34:33.615 --> 00:34:34.695
Says the horse.

00:34:34.755 --> 00:34:36.477
He doesn't want to work.

00:34:36.537 --> 00:34:37.827
Says the ox.

00:34:37.888 --> 00:34:42.140
He just eats and sleeps and says humph.

00:34:42.200 --> 00:34:43.892
Says the dog.

00:34:43.952 --> 00:34:49.646
The farmer thinks for a moment and then says, You three must work more then.

00:34:49.706 --> 00:34:50.236
What?

00:34:50.256 --> 00:34:50.807
What?

00:34:50.867 --> 00:34:54.569
The animals say, We don't want to work more.

00:34:54.629 --> 00:34:59.451
You must work more because the camel doesn't want to work.

00:34:59.511 --> 00:35:01.332
Says the farmer.

00:35:01.392 --> 00:35:07.234
The horse, the ox and the dog are very angry and they start talking.

00:35:07.294 --> 00:35:10.346
The camel walks by and listens to them.

00:35:10.406 --> 00:35:11.847
Hump.

00:35:11.907 --> 00:35:15.808
Says the camel and goes away laughing.

00:35:15.868 --> 00:35:18.550
The animals don't know what to do.

00:35:18.610 --> 00:35:20.001
We need help.

00:35:20.061 --> 00:35:21.252
Says the horse.

00:35:21.312 --> 00:35:22.418
Yes.

00:35:22.478 --> 00:35:24.446
says the dog sadly.

00:35:24.506 --> 00:35:26.818
But who can help us?

00:35:26.878 --> 00:35:31.674
Suddenly, the desert magician arrives on a big cloud.

00:35:31.734 --> 00:35:35.147
He is a great magician and lives in the desert.

00:35:35.208 --> 00:35:37.610
He is everyone's friend.

00:35:37.670 --> 00:35:38.722
Hello?

00:35:38.782 --> 00:35:39.712
He says.

00:35:39.772 --> 00:35:41.772
What are you talking about?

00:35:41.832 --> 00:35:43.642
Why are you angry?

00:35:43.702 --> 00:35:45.653
Oh, desert magician.

00:35:45.713 --> 00:35:46.853
Says the horse.

00:35:46.914 --> 00:35:48.854
We have a big problem.

00:35:48.915 --> 00:35:50.605
What's your problem?

00:35:50.665 --> 00:35:52.696
Asks the desert magician.

00:35:52.756 --> 00:35:54.297
Tell me about it.

00:35:54.357 --> 00:35:58.069
The camel in the desert doesn't want to work.

00:35:58.129 --> 00:35:59.480
Says the horse.

00:35:59.540 --> 00:36:02.141
Why doesn't he want to work?

00:36:02.201 --> 00:36:04.632
Asks the desert magician.

00:36:04.692 --> 00:36:06.253
He's lazy.

00:36:06.313 --> 00:36:07.594
Says the ox.

00:36:07.654 --> 00:36:08.614
Yes.

00:36:08.674 --> 00:36:09.925
Says the horse.

00:36:09.985 --> 00:36:11.594
Very lazy.

00:36:11.654 --> 00:36:15.626
And we must do more work, says the dog.

00:36:15.687 --> 00:36:18.540
We already work hard all day long.

00:36:18.600 --> 00:36:20.192
Says the ox.

00:36:20.252 --> 00:36:22.804
What does the camel say?

00:36:22.864 --> 00:36:25.267
Asks the desert magician.

00:36:25.327 --> 00:36:28.240
He always says humph.

00:36:28.301 --> 00:36:29.862
Says the horse.

00:36:29.922 --> 00:36:32.835
I must go and talk to the camel.

00:36:32.895 --> 00:36:35.348
Says the desert magician.

00:36:35.408 --> 00:36:42.022
The desert magician's magic cloud carries him to the desert and he sees the camel.

00:36:42.082 --> 00:36:45.073
He is standing near a pool of water.

00:36:45.133 --> 00:36:48.454
Why don't you want to work, camel?

00:36:48.514 --> 00:36:50.705
Asks the desert magician.

00:36:50.765 --> 00:36:52.376
Hence.

00:36:52.436 --> 00:36:56.396
Says the camel, looking at the pool of water.

00:36:56.456 --> 00:37:01.718
The other animals must work more because you don't work.

00:37:01.778 --> 00:37:04.547
Says the desert magician.

00:37:04.607 --> 00:37:06.996
says the camel.

00:37:07.056 --> 00:37:10.178
Don't say humph.

00:37:10.238 --> 00:37:12.300
Says the desert magician.

00:37:12.360 --> 00:37:15.082
You must start working.

00:37:15.142 --> 00:37:19.356
The camel looks at himself in the pool of water.

00:37:19.417 --> 00:37:22.408
I'm a great magician.

00:37:22.468 --> 00:37:24.420
Thinks the desert magician.

00:37:24.480 --> 00:37:27.172
What magic can I do?

00:37:27.232 --> 00:37:31.082
The camel must work.

00:37:31.142 --> 00:37:36.161
The desert magician sits down and thinks about something magic.

00:37:36.221 --> 00:37:40.672
Suddenly the camel has a big hump on his back.

00:37:40.732 --> 00:37:43.593
He looks in the pool of water and sees it.

00:37:43.653 --> 00:37:45.874
He is very surprised.

00:37:45.934 --> 00:37:48.094
What's that on my back?

00:37:48.154 --> 00:37:50.745
He asks the desert magician.

00:37:50.805 --> 00:37:53.346
It's your hump.

00:37:53.406 --> 00:37:55.806
Says the desert magician.

00:37:55.866 --> 00:37:59.197
I don't like it and I don't want it.

00:37:59.258 --> 00:38:01.679
Says the camel angrily.

00:38:01.740 --> 00:38:05.393
How can I work with this hump on my back?

00:38:05.454 --> 00:38:08.936
Now you can work more than the other animals.

00:38:08.996 --> 00:38:10.908
Says the desert magician.

00:38:10.968 --> 00:38:12.370
With your hump?

00:38:12.430 --> 00:38:16.813
You don't need to eat or drink for three days.

00:38:16.873 --> 00:38:17.724
What?

00:38:17.784 --> 00:38:19.916
Says the camel angrily.

00:38:19.976 --> 00:38:22.338
I don't want to work.

00:38:22.398 --> 00:38:27.722
Now be quiet and start working.

00:38:27.783 --> 00:38:30.353
Says the desert magician.

00:38:30.413 --> 00:38:35.453
The camel walks away slowly and joins the other animals.

00:38:35.514 --> 00:38:40.846
When the other animals see him, they laugh and laugh.

00:38:40.906 --> 00:38:47.162
On that day the camel starts working, but he still isn't friendly.

